          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "AKA osteochondrosis of tibial tubercle - common overuse condition in active prepubertal adolescents"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 0,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tibial tubercle = secondary ossification center - begins to ossify around adolescent growth spurt (girls 10-13y · boys 12-15y) - often hx of recent rapid growth"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 0,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "PATHO: repeated quad contract (running · cutting · jumping) → tension on patellar tendon → strain @ tibial tubercle apophysis → chronic avulsion - ossified portion pulls away & fibrous/fibrocartilaginous tissue fills defect - apophysis eventually ossifies & fuses but may → markedly enlrg tibial tubercle"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
